<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attar-shumki I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 800 BCE</span> · Also known as Attarshumki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Attar-shumki I was king of Arpad, the Aramaean state of Bit-Agusi in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, around 800 BCE. He led a coalition of north Syrian kings against the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adad-nirari-iii">Adad-nirari III</a>, which was defeated. The Sefire treaty names the later king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matiilu">Mati'ilu</a> as a son of Attar-shumki.</p></div>
